@page "/"

<PageTitle>SLIP-39 + age wallet backup</PageTitle>

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h1 class="text-white">🔐 SLIP-39 + age wallet backup</h1>
        <p class="lead text-muted">
            Secure your BIP-39 wallet with threshold secret-sharing and age encryption.
            100% client-side, safe for offline Tails use.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-4 justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-md-5">
            <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body text-center p-4">
                    <h2 class="card-title h4 mb-3">📤 Create backup</h2>
                    <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                        Enter your seed words, choose a threshold, and the tool produces a single
                        dated backup zip containing your SLIP-39 share folders and the
                        encrypted <code>payload.age</code> blob.
                    </p>
                    <a href="/owner" class="btn btn-primary mt-3">Start backup →</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-5">
            <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body text-center p-4">
                    <h2 class="card-title h4 mb-3">📥 Recover wallet</h2>
                    <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                        Gather threshold-many SLIP-39 mnemonics and the <code>payload.age</code>
                        ciphertext, then reconstruct your seed words and passphrase here.
                    </p>
                    <a href="/recoverer" class="btn btn-success mt-3">Start recovery →</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-5">
        <small class="text-muted">
            Phase 1 backend tests pass. Phase 2 wires this UI to the core library.
            See <a href="https://github.com/PeteSparrowBTC/Seed-Phrase-Storage-SLIP39" class="text-info">the repo</a>
            for the spec and recovery procedure.
        </small>
    </div>
</div>
